    "type": "question",
    "label": "11",
    "prompt": "Simplify each expression. Check your answer for part a by substituting $x=2$ into both the original expression and the simplified expression. Repeat for $x=3$ in part b and $x=-2$ in part c.",
    "layout": "grid",
    "columns": 4,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p7-q11-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "$\\frac{6x^2}{x}$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$6x$. At $x=2$, both expressions equal $12$.",
          "worked": "$\\begin{align*}\\frac{6x^2}{x}&=6x^{2-1}\\\\\\frac{6x^2}{x}&=6x\\end{align*}$\n\nAt $x=2$:\n\n$\\begin{align*}\\frac{6(2)^2}{2}&=\\frac{24}{2}\\\\\\frac{6(2)^2}{2}&=12\\\\6(2)&=12\\end{align*}$\n\nBoth expressions equal $12$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 33
      },
      {
        "id": "p7-q11-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "$\\frac{6x^2}{3x}$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$2x$. At $x=3$, both expressions equal $6$.",
          "worked": "$\\begin{align*}\\frac{6x^2}{3x}&=2x^{2-1}\\\\\\frac{6x^2}{3x}&=2x\\end{align*}$\n\nAt $x=3$:\n\n$\\begin{align*}\\frac{6(3)^2}{3(3)}&=\\frac{54}{9}\\\\\\frac{6(3)^2}{3(3)}&=6\\\\2(3)&=6\\end{align*}$\n\nBoth expressions equal $6$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 33
      },
      {
        "id": "p7-q11-c",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "c",
        "prompt": "$\\frac{6x^2}{6x}$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$x$. At $x=-2$, both expressions equal $-2$.",
          "worked": "$\\begin{align*}\\frac{6x^2}{6x}&=x^{2-1}\\\\\\frac{6x^2}{6x}&=x\\end{align*}$\n\nAt $x=-2$:\n\n$\\begin{align*}\\frac{6(-2)^2}{6(-2)}&=\\frac{24}{-12}\\\\\\frac{6(-2)^2}{6(-2)}&=-2\\\\x&=-2\\end{align*}$\n\nBoth expressions equal $-2$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 33
      },
      {
        "id": "p7-q11-d",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "d",
        "prompt": "$\\frac{8x^4}{4x}$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$2x^3$",
          "worked": "$\\begin{align*}\\frac{8x^4}{4x}&=2x^{4-1}\\\\\\frac{8x^4}{4x}&=2x^3\\end{align*}$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 16
      },
      {
        "id": "p7-q11-e",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "e",
        "prompt": "$\\frac{3x^5}{x^3}$",
